sequenceDiagram
    participant O as Human job owner
    participant G as Gate orchestrator
    participant S as Durable run store
    participant C1 as Codex attempt one
    participant P as Behavior observer
    participant R as Evidence reviewer
    participant C2 as Codex attempt two

    O->>G: Supply authoritative brief
    G->>C1: Send first coding prompt
    C1-->>G: Return generated handler
    G->>P: Execute handler calls
    P-->>G: Return normalized outcomes
    G->>S: Persist attempt and observation
    alt Every outcome has approved coverage
        loop Each observed outcome
            G->>R: Send brief and observed behavior
            R-->>G: Return evidence classification
        end
        G-->>O: Pause with two decision requests
        O->>G: Record administrator answer
        G-->>O: Remain paused with one request
        O->>G: Record repeated request answer
        G->>C2: Send fresh prompt with both answers
        C2-->>G: Return regenerated handler
        G->>P: Execute the same handler calls
        P-->>G: Return regenerated outcomes
        G->>G: Compare every expected outcome
        G-->>O: Return COMPLETED or FAILED
    else Any outcome is unmodeled
        G->>S: Mark run as COVERAGE_GAP
        Note over S: Available for later platform engineering review
        G-->>O: Stop without product decision or retry
    end
